<title>USA: Calif. measure may disrupt part of market-Moody's.</title>
<headline>Calif. measure may disrupt part of market-Moody's.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>A controversial California tax measure approved by voters in November could disrupt a portion of the municipal market, a Moody's Investors Service Inc vice president warned on Thursday.</p>
<p>Moody's Vice President Ken Kurtz told a teleconference for institutional investors that the credit implications of Proposition 218 will not be devastating, but warned there may be a few &quot;ticking time-bombs&quot; that could affect the market.</p>
<p>The intent of Proposition 218 was to ensure that all taxes and most charges on property owners are subject to voter approval.</p>
</text>
